-- title:
--   Maximality of the two special-fibre component generic points
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of `DRModelPackage p`, i.e. a bundle of data and properties for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` $=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) over $\mathbb{Z}$ attached to the modular function field of level $p$ and the Igusa function `IgusaScheme.jFull p`, with structural morphism `DRModel.toBase p` to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$; among the components of that bundle are a curve model `𝔛.ratModel κ` over each field $\kappa$ and two morphisms `𝔛.compInf κ`, `𝔛.compZero κ` from its underlying scheme $(\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{ratModel}\,\kappa).C$ to the pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb{Z}\to\kappa$. Let $O$ be a local ring whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Write $\xi_\infty$, respectively $\xi_0$, for the image of the generic point of $(\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{ratModel}\,\kappa).C$ under the map of underlying spaces of `𝔛.compInf κ`, respectively `𝔛.compZero κ`, followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`, a point of the pullback $P$ of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb{Z}\to O$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two statements: for $\xi = \xi_\infty$ and for $\xi = \xi_0$, every point $y$ of $P$ lying outside the preimage under the second projection $P \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ of the basic open set $D(p)$, and such that $\xi$ lies in the closure of $\{y\}$, equals $\xi$.
--
--   The assertion is that $\xi_\infty$ and $\xi_0$ admit no strict generalisation inside the fibre over $(p)$, so each is the generic point of an irreducible component of that fibre; this is the form in which the two components of the Deligne–Rapoport special fibre of the model of level $p$ are pinned down over an arbitrary local base with maximal ideal $(p)$. It is used in the comparison of branch ideals on the model, in the analogous statement for the first projection, and in producing residue-field points of the base change.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackage_eq_baseChangeMap_genericPoint_of_specializes.lean

